<xml>
  <block type="device_oled_spi" x="30" y="30">
    <mutation uid="oled10" />
    <field name="NAME">screen</field>
    <field name="CS">10</field>
    <field name="DC">9</field>
    <field name="RESET">8</field>
    <comment pinned="false" w="390" h="170">Purpose: Count seconds on an SSD1306 SPI OLED using a named device and no framebuffer. Update with millis timing.
Wiring: SSD1306 SPI OLED: CS D10, DC D9, RESET D8; SPI MOSI D11, SCK D13; MISO is unused; CS/DC/RESET as listed. Common GND; use each module’s required supply.
Try: Edit the heading or move the counter to another text row.</comment>
  </block>
  <block type="arduino_typed_variable" x="510" y="30">
    <field name="VAR">lastSample</field>
    <field name="TYPE">uint32_t</field>
    <value name="VALUE">
      <block type="math_number">
        <field name="NUM">0</field>
      </block>
    </value>
  </block>
  <block type="arduino_typed_variable" x="990" y="30">
    <field name="VAR">seconds</field>
    <field name="TYPE">uint32_t</field>
    <value name="VALUE">
      <block type="math_number">
        <field name="NUM">0</field>
      </block>
    </value>
  </block>
  <block type="arduino_setup_section" x="30" y="290">
    <statement name="DO">
      <block type="device_oled_print">
        <field name="DEVICE">oled10</field>
        <value name="TEXT">
          <block type="text">
            <field name="TEXT">Tiny RAM, big fun</field>
          </block>
        </value>
        <value name="COL">
          <block type="math_number">
            <field name="NUM">0</field>
          </block>
        </value>
        <value name="ROW">
          <block type="math_number">
            <field name="NUM">0</field>
          </block>
        </value>
      </block>
    </statement>
    <comment pinned="false" w="390" h="170">Initialize the named SPI OLED once and write a heading. Text coordinates are character cells: columns 0–15, rows 0–7.</comment>
  </block>
  <block type="arduino_loop_section" x="510" y="290">
    <statement name="DO">
      <block type="controls_if">
        <value name="IF0">
          <block type="logic_compare">
            <field name="OP">GTE</field>
            <value name="A">
              <block type="math_arithmetic">
                <field name="OP">MINUS</field>
                <value name="A">
                  <block type="arduino_millis" />
                </value>
                <value name="B">
                  <block type="variables_get">
                    <field name="VAR">lastSample</field>
                  </block>
                </value>
              </block>
            </value>
            <value name="B">
              <block type="math_number">
                <field name="NUM">1000</field>
              </block>
            </value>
          </block>
        </value>
        <statement name="DO0">
          <block type="variables_set">
            <field name="VAR">lastSample</field>
            <value name="VALUE">
              <block type="arduino_millis" />
            </value>
            <next>
              <block type="device_oled_print">
                <field name="DEVICE">oled10</field>
                <value name="TEXT">
                  <block type="variables_get">
                    <field name="VAR">seconds</field>
                  </block>
                </value>
                <value name="COL">
                  <block type="math_number">
                    <field name="NUM">0</field>
                  </block>
                </value>
                <value name="ROW">
                  <block type="math_number">
                    <field name="NUM">3</field>
                  </block>
                </value>
                <next>
                  <block type="variables_set">
                    <field name="VAR">seconds</field>
                    <value name="VALUE">
                      <block type="math_arithmetic">
                        <field name="OP">ADD</field>
                        <value name="A">
                          <block type="variables_get">
                            <field name="VAR">seconds</field>
                          </block>
                        </value>
                        <value name="B">
                          <block type="math_number">
                            <field name="NUM">1</field>
                          </block>
                        </value>
                      </block>
                    </value>
                  </block>
                </next>
              </block>
            </next>
          </block>
        </statement>
        <comment pinned="false" w="390" h="170">Use elapsed milliseconds instead of delay. The command reader remains responsive between updates; unsigned subtraction also works when millis wraps.</comment>
      </block>
    </statement>
    <comment pinned="false" w="390" h="170">Update the seconds counter once per second. For pixel patterns see the packed-buffer lesson; small tiles work on ATmega168.</comment>
  </block>
</xml>
